                    :location (b / behind
                        :op1 (s / string-entity
                            :value "as-well")))))
        :mod (a / any))
    :mode imperative)

# ::tok If only part of the four steps (Preprocess, Compile, Compile, Connect) is operated, the ∀ -x' option (or Ah after the filename) can be used to tell geo where to begin, and the ∀~-c', `-s', or `-E' option to tell geo where to end. Note that certain combinations of options (e.g., ∀-x cpp-output-E') {i gee MEF =c compile or compile a source file, ETER. In the absence of the ERA ATI, GCC uses a ▽.o' by replacing the source file name after the file name in the ∀.ec file name label. Other options can be used to choose a name.
